.TH "RTCERROR.SDPLINENUMBER" "3JS" "August 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCError.sdpLineNumber \- RTCError: sdpLineNumber property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]sdpLineNumber\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]RTCError\f[R] interface specifies the SDP message line number
where a syntax error occurred.
.SH VALUE
An integer value indicating the SDP message line number where the syntax
error described by the \f[CR]RTCError\f[R] object occurred.
The lines are numbered starting with line 1.
.PP
This property is \f[CR]null\f[R] unless the value of
\f[CR]errorDetail\f[R] is \f[CR]sdp\-syntax\-error\f[R].
